<title>USA: US budget deal good for growth,low inflation-Rubin.</title>
<headline>US budget deal good for growth,low inflation-Rubin.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said the budget agreement reached with Congress on Friday would help keep interest rates at levels that would extend the current performance of the economy.</p>
<p>The effect of the agreement would be to &quot;maintain an interest rate environment that is conducive to solid growth and I think also tend to produce low inflation,&quot; he told CNN.</p>
<p>He declined to say what the effect the budget agreement would have on the dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;We've had a very sound policy towards the dollar, and we'll continue with our policy,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>((-- Washington Newsroom (202) 898-8300))</p>
